# 20｜Vertical Slice Governance
A project is not required to finish every PI/PD package before the first eligible slice executes. Eligibility is slice-scoped.
`SliceEligible = required_PI_dependency_closure_complete ∧ applicable_PI_READY ∧ required_PD_binding_PREDEV_READY ∧ slice_specific_TQAEP_construction_ready ∧ exact_ExecutionAdmission=ADMIT`
Additional constitutional checks apply when slices share a canonical writer, non-partitionable permission/resource, invalidation edge, rollback boundary or unresolved cross-slice contract. In those cases concurrency may be blocked for the coupled scope only.
|Condition|Required?|Owner of fact|Failure route|
|---|---|---|---|
|Required PI dependency closure|Yes|DOC-02 + dependency graph|Keep slice in PI/PD; unaffected slices continue|
|Applicable `PI_READY`|Yes|DOC-02 facts; DOC-01 state semantics|No PD execution path|
|Required PD binding / `PREDEV_READY`|Yes|DOC-03|No admission request|
|Slice TQAEP construction-ready|Yes|DOC-03/04/07|No admission request|
|Exact `ExecutionAdmission=ADMIT`|Yes for first mutation|DOC-05|DENY/HOLD; no mutation|
|All unrelated project packages complete|No|N/A|Must not be invented as global waterfall gate|
