Join rules:
1. `human_approval_ref` resolves to one canonical token-store record.
2. Canonicalized embedded token bytes hash to `token_digest`; mismatch is `DENY/TOKEN_DIGEST_MISMATCH`.
3. `scope_digest` is computed from canonical sorted scope; a widened/reordered semantic scope cannot evade comparison.
4. Nonce consumption is an **atomic compare-and-set** from `ISSUED → CONSUMED` when an `ADMIT` is issued. Failure to consume is `DENY/NONCE_ALREADY_USED`.
5. Revocation or expiry propagates through reverse dependencies to `AdmissionValidityRecord.status=INVALIDATED/STALE` for affected admissions only.
6. A token cannot be copied into a second admission after consumption; a new operation/scope/hash requires a new token.
7. Maker self-approval is rejected for ASSURED/high-risk and whenever policy requires SoD.
This closes reference/embed ambiguity and makes replay/revocation machine-decidable.

