## 16.3 CUSTOM acceptance
- canonical extension validates A2 schema with `additionalProperties:false`;
- projection resolves to that canonical extension and an existing base target;
- `core_override=false`;
- added contracts are strictly additive;
- base target and weight remain visible in ProfileBinding;
- extension removal/invalidation cannot orphan tests/oracles or silently change semantics.
# 17｜Applicability / Reasoned N/A / Tailoring Rules
Every denominator item is first classified as:
- `PROFILE_MANDATORY_NEVER_NA`: may encode an explicit empty/deny/none semantic value, but field/contract cannot disappear;
- `CONDITIONAL_WITH_PREDICATE`: may be `NOT_APPLICABLE` only if the stated predicate is evaluated, evidenced and version-bound.
A valid reasoned N/A record MUST include requirement ID, predicate, actual fact/evidence, decision owner/time, and invalidation trigger. “not needed”, “low risk”, “later”, missing implementation, lack of data, or desire to reduce documents are invalid rationales.
| Family | Mandatory-never-NA examples | Conditionally applicable examples |
|---|---|---|
| SYSTEM | Product outcome, Architecture, Security/Privacy, Acceptance/Testability, ProfileBinding | API only when no interface; data when no persisted/exchanged data; migration when verified greenfield; operability/SLO for non-runtime only |
| SKILL_PLUGIN | PI18 denominator fields remain present; allowed_tools may be `[]`, network may be `DENY`, effects may be `NONE` | PD concrete bindings for a capability that truly does not exist may be `NOT_USED` with evidence/recheck |
| AGENT_HARNESS | identity, loop, context, permission, guardrail/eval/evidence responsibilities | specific interop protocol or persistent memory backend can be `NOT_USED`; base boundary still present |
| Brownfield | all 12 steps once specialization enabled | specialization itself disabled only with evidence of no incumbent/migration surface |
| CUSTOM | A2 canonical fields all required | individual added contracts may be conditional only by their own explicit predicate |
